Subject: [PATCH] claude: Mark claims as fact or inference
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: snyntntlokprpkpyqqonplmqzqpyxorr

An inference reported as a fact reads the same as a checked one, so
the reader cannot tell which claims to trust. Reporting notmuch-emacs
as missing was such a case: a failed load was taken as the cause,
when one pkg query would have shown the package installed. Asking
for the evidence, not a label, keeps the check where the reader can
repeat it, since the model writes any label it is told to add.
